ompensation."],"hlth":["The company holds more cash than debt.","No distress or manipulation flags (Altman Z 7.0, in the safe zone)."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at 6.7% over 3 years, 15.0% over 5 years and 12.2% over 10 years, so growth is decelerating, and it has been lumpy (year-to-year swings of 16%).","Net reinvestment is nil (capex and working capital no more than cover depreciation), so fundamental growth is near zero.","Free cash flow has compounded 10.2% a year over five years.","Forward indicators: deferred revenue up 16%.","Capex roughly matches depreciation (1.4x, 3.5% of sales), a maintenance pace.","Its Rule of 40 score is 23, below the 40 that marks a healthy growth business."],"own":["Insiders hold little stock (0.2%), and reported institutional holdings exceed 100% of shares (a sign of heavy share lending).","It returns 3.2% a year to shareholders (3.2% in buybacks).","The share count has shrunk 4.6% a year over five years, steadily raising each holder's stake."],"people":["With about 21,382 employees, each generates about $580K of revenue, 1.5x the Consumer Cyclical median, and revenue has grown 14.9% a year across its filed history.","That works out to $50K of free cash flow per employee.","CEO pay is $5.8M (10x revenue per employee), and compensation governance scores poorly (9/10, lower is better).","Stock compensation averages $2K per employee."]},"profile":{"v":"WATCH","conv":63,"head":"Watch: composite 59, above the 57 line, but no margin of safety; it becomes a buy below $557.","pros":["Composite 59, above the 57 line (gates 12/26)","ROIC 93.4% vs WACC 8.8%","Revenue grew 15.0%/yr over 5y","Net debt/EBITDA -0.3x","Altman Z in the safe zone"],"cons":["Trades 1% above fair value of $655","P/E 24.1x vs sector 18.8x","EV/EBITDA 15.6x vs sector 10.7x","P/FCF 26.5x vs sector 16.7x"],"flags":[],"need":["no margin of safety"],"buy_below":556.96,"vc":{"base":655.25,"base_src":"dcf","bear":502.04,"bull":860.83,"alt_median":439.8,"n_alt":2,"gap"